An EVB message<pre><code>{
  "measurements": [
    {
      "name": "TemperatureHumidity",
      "tags": {"plant": "StreamdaqFactory", "unit_id": "012332"},
      "type": "Points",
      "fields": ["time", "temperature", "humidity"],
      "values": [
        [1645334535000, 60, 55],
        [1645338135000, 62, 54]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> Part Meaning <code>fields</code> The column names. The first one must be <code>time</code>. <code>values</code> One list per reading, in the same order as <code>fields</code>. The time is in epoch milliseconds (13 digits). <code>tags</code> Text labels that apply to all readings of the measurement, e.g. the plant and unit. <code>type</code> <code>Points</code>, <code>Report</code>, <code>Metadata</code>, <code>State</code>, <code>Configuration</code> or <code>Unknown</code>.

tasks.json<pre><code>[{
  "name": "readings",
  "input": {
    "type": "jsonlines",
    "params": {"path": "readings.jsonl", "schema": {"timestamp": "int", "unit_id": "str", "temperature": "float"}}
  },
  "output": {"type": "jsonlines", "params": {"filename": "quality.jsonl"}},
  "wait_for_late": 5,
  "instant_checks": [
    {"name": "valid_temperature", "check_class": "InRange", "params": {"column": "temperature", "low": -30, "high": 50}}
  ],
  "window_checks_config": {
    "windowby_column": "timestamp",
    "groupby_column": "unit_id",
    "window": {"type": "tumbling", "params": {"duration": 60}},
    "checks": [
      {"name": "enough_readings", "measure": {"type": "Count", "params": {"column": "temperature"}}, "must_be": "&gt;= 5"},
      {"name": "mean_temperature", "measure": {"type": "Mean", "params": {"column": "temperature", "precision": 2}}}
    ]
  }
}]
</code></pre>
